about:
I have almost 20 years experience with PwC, in both our Assurance & Deals practices, spending time in Manchester, Chicago and now London. 3 fantastic cities. 

I lead a team that helps our clients maximise value from deals. This includes strategy, planning, operations, people, tax, and accounting. I focus my time on complex carve outs and cross-border M&A, specialising in project managing these complex deals, with a particular focus on the accounting and public reporting considerations.

I have a significant amount of transaction and listings experience, having worked on a number of high profile transactions across the globe. These include IPOs, cross-border M&A, GAAP conversions, carve outs, and public capital raises. Some of my completed transaction include:

- Unilever’s $7b divestment of its Spreads Business;
- Imperial Brands’ $7b acquisition of certain brands from Reynolds and Lorillard;
- Reckitt Benckiser’s $4b divestment of its Food Business;
- GE Capital’s €1b divestment of its Fleet Business;
- INEOS’ joint venture (and subsequent buyout) with Solvay; and
- Acadia Healthcare’s acquisitions of Priory Group and Partnerships In Care.

I work across multiple sectors, with both listed groups and privately owned businesses (including private equity owned).

Outside of work, I enjoy keeping fit, having run the London, Chicago, Paris & Valencia marathons. I have also swum, biked and ran several Olympic and Half Ironman distance triathlons. I am a keen rugby fan and make the effort to get to the majority of Wales’ home games in Cardiff.

Specialities: carveouts, carve-outs, carve outs, divestments, M&A, IPO, acquisitions, capital markets, accounting, IFRS, debt offerings, high yield

